Host script
nvidia-proxmox-host.sh host-install — installs/updates the host NVIDIA stack and saves the detected host driver version to /etc/nvidia-host-version; run this first on the Proxmox host.

nvidia-proxmox-host.sh detect — shows detected /dev/nvidia* devices and the passthrough block it would generate; use it to sanity-check the host before applying CT config.

nvidia-proxmox-host.sh ct-apply <ctid...> — adds or refreshes the NVIDIA passthrough block in one or more CT configs under /etc/pve/lxc/.

nvidia-proxmox-host.sh push-version <ctid...> — copies /etc/nvidia-host-version into one or more containers.

nvidia-proxmox-host.sh push-ct-script <ctid...> — copies /root/nvidia-proxmox-ct.sh into one or more containers and makes it executable.

CT script
/root/nvidia-proxmox-ct.sh install — cleans old NVIDIA/CUDA state, adds the correct NVIDIA repo for Debian 11/12/13, and installs CT userspace packages matching the host driver version; use this for both new containers and updating old ones.

/root/nvidia-proxmox-ct.sh cleanup — removes old NVIDIA/CUDA packages and repo config; usually not needed before install because install already runs cleanup internally.

/root/nvidia-proxmox-ct.sh verify — runs nvidia-smi and nvcc --version inside the container to confirm the setup.

Example usage:
Update existing setup
On the host:

bash /root/nvidia-proxmox-host.sh host-install
bash /root/nvidia-proxmox-host.sh ct-apply 101 102
bash /root/nvidia-proxmox-host.sh push-version 101 102
bash /root/nvidia-proxmox-host.sh push-ct-script 101 102

Then for each CT:

pct exec 101 -- bash /root/nvidia-proxmox-ct.sh install
pct exec 102 -- bash /root/nvidia-proxmox-ct.sh install

Install on new containers
For a new container, use the same flow after the CT exists:

bash /root/nvidia-proxmox-host.sh ct-apply 105
bash /root/nvidia-proxmox-host.sh push-version 105
bash /root/nvidia-proxmox-host.sh push-ct-script 105
pct exec 105 -- bash /root/nvidia-proxmox-ct.sh install
pct exec 105 -- bash /root/nvidia-proxmox-ct.sh verify

